<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>France among five major powers to represent EU in Ukraine talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab96867ed3181a681db25418f7218296861eab8c3ee2a9ca8876fd705759f164</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:38:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-europe-to-send-diplomats-from-across-the-continent-to-ukraine-peace-talks--44eded81bb78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-europe-to-send-diplomats-from-across-the-continent-to-ukraine-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">European Council President Antonio Costa on Friday said that Brussels will send diplomats from the bloc and five countries, including the UK, France, Germany, Italy and Poland, to upcoming Ukraine talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The Downfall of AI’s ‘Rock Star’ Boss, Ukraine: Who speaks for Europe? Protests &amp; Presidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39b4bf95348693b93255af93aa9f8f6fdd1661be66ed67adefe196bf1f1c8310</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261113-the-downfall-of-ai-s-rock-star-boss-ukraine-who-speak-for-europe-protests-presidents--795148188632.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261113-the-downfall-of-ai-s-rock-star-boss-ukraine-who-speak-for-europe-protests-presidents" /><summary type="html">On The World This Week with Gavin Lee, our panel distills the breaking news and global stories of the past 7 days into 45 minutes. 
 
Ukraine: Who will speak for Europe?
 
In a week thats seen the first direct talks between Ukraine and Russia since February, with the US in the room and the Europeans relegated to the lobby according to Moscow. A new ‘European Security Architecture’ is discussed.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Hurry up and wait: Europe wants a place at the table, ‘must make up its mind’ over Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bd33df30995de758cc7afb79bf44675e27cd9e88de39989923b548d3ee76471</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:03:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261113-hurry-up-and-wait-europe-wants-a-place-at-the-table-must-make-up-its-mind-over-ukraine--0ede6861b758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261113-hurry-up-and-wait-europe-wants-a-place-at-the-table-must-make-up-its-mind-over-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Alexander Titov, Lecturer in Modern European History at Queen's University Belfast and a specialist on Russia. He's joined us to discuss high-level meetings in Abu Dhabi, Dublin and the prospects for ending the war in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>'We have done all our homework' to get EU candidate status: Kosovo's PM Albin Kurti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11b1eb367dc48ead1342dc0c66cf8c3cb0bd0a031aebf24124d1a5e6391c1c6c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:46:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261113-we-have-done-all-our-homework-to-get-eu-candidate-status-kosovo-s-pm-albin-kurti--597ebf8d6a3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261113-we-have-done-all-our-homework-to-get-eu-candidate-status-kosovo-s-pm-albin-kurti" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24 hosts Albin Kurti, the prime minister of Kosovo, a country that declared its independence from Serbia back in 2008 and sees itself as part of the European family. But four years after applying to join the EU, Kosovo has still not received candidate status. We explore Kosovo's path towards the EU, and the broader European and regional dynamics surrounding that.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>As EU grapples with fierce AI competition, summit overshadowed by elusive Ukraine-Russia peace deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaeca48e09cd43d345ef821dfc1c21a428fd0b47d5c8ae8ce395cfda4647785f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-as-eu-grapples-with-fierce-ai-competition-summit-overshadowed-by-elusive-ukraine-russia-pea--d418c75912c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-as-eu-grapples-with-fierce-ai-competition-summit-overshadowed-by-elusive-ukraine-russia-peace-deal-1" /><summary type="html">As EU leaders meet for an AI summit in Dublin, largely overshadowed by Russia's war on Ukraine, William Hilderbrandt is pleased to welcome Fabrice Pothier, CEO of Rasmussen Global. On AI, Pothier points to Europe's limited computing capacity, estimating that it barely represents "5% of what's available out there." Despite the EU's wealth of researchers and expertise, he warns that Europe is struggling to turn these resources into "real technological and industrial scale." Now, turning to the war in Ukraine, Pothier argues that European governments should focus less on "whether they have a place at the table" and more on "making Ukraine's hands stronger," particularly by providing additional air defence interceptors.</summary></entry><entry><title>November 13 Paris attacks: Eleven years later, France pays tribute to victims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daef8c884f5714977a0f94b3950f12738d41a7ea98960e25b57b2d9e0399c08f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:47:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/november-13-paris-attacks-eleven-years-later-france-pays-tribute-to-victims--43a7704539a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/november-13-paris-attacks-eleven-years-later-france-pays-tribute-to-victims" /><summary type="html">Eleven years on, France pays tribute to the victims of the November 13 attacks. French officials, victims’ associations and families gathered this Friday to pay their respects to those killed in the attacks in Paris on November 13, 2015.</summary></entry><entry><title>West Bank: ‘Without international trade and financial support, large settlements would not exist’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:181c22274ec783ef2acb62c3904b199ee58cd81694da1e6cbced2b4c466e2462</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:15:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exi--ca01d4fe66ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exist-1" /><summary type="html">France is considering legislation to restrict trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories, namely the West Bank. Ivar Ekeland, Professor Emeritus at Paris Dauphine-PSL University and Chair of the Organization of Academics for the Respect of International Law in Palestine, discusses the proposed measures with Alison Sargent. He calls for restrictions to cover n ot only goods but also services, including financial services, insurance and tourism. "Without the support of financial entities, of insurance, of providing goods and so on, settlements, big settlements, would not exist," he argues.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes targets across Ukraine as Kyiv launches nearly 1,200 drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4509748e31b422cd32e7d5435fb1c1fb5005e9cbff5044d60ea0355c3d7448e9</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:46:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-russian-airstrikes-continue-ukraine-launches-nearly-1-200-drones--8c91678fb217.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-russian-airstrikes-continue-ukraine-launches-nearly-1-200-drones" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes hit targets across Ukraine on Thursday, with one attack damaging a hospital. Ukraine meanwhile fired almost 1,200 drones at Russian targets overnight in one of its biggest aerial attacks since Moscow’s full-scale invasion nearly five years ago.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK rocked by comedians' sex scandals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02ff60952b371a806fc97201fb6a07663d6077743beadc1d4b334016a266ad82</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T13:47:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261113-uk-rocked-by-comedians-sex-scandals--23c096cd618a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261113-uk-rocked-by-comedians-sex-scandals" /><summary type="html">The UK is facing a reckoning in the world of entertainment, as two well-known comedy figures find themselves at the centre of serious allegations and headlines. This as Russell Brand is jailed for more than 10 years after being found guilty of rape and sexual assault and David Walliams faces serious allegations of sexual misconduct.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>US, Ukraine say Europe to join peace talks as Putin sticks to hardline stance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7883ad9c6e22fa1d68e54dffee5f86f6b6a6a943e2c7aa9992db4a8bf146faa9</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:59:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-us-ukraine-say-europe-to-join-peace-talks-as-putin-sticks-to-hardline-stance--85a4661b19a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-us-ukraine-say-europe-to-join-peace-talks-as-putin-sticks-to-hardline-stance" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky and US envoy Jared Kushner said Thursday, November 12, Europe would join the next round of talks with Russia, as Vladimir Putin indicated Moscow will not compromise on its hardline demands to end almost five years of war. In a packed day of shuttle diplomacy following negotiations in Abu Dhabi, Kushner and fellow envoy Steve Witkoff held over four hours of talks with Putin in the Kremlin before jetting to debrief Zelensky in Dublin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Winter is coming: Putin seeks to 'hammer Ukrainians, their power grid, their water supplies'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e8c745450df37cbe21e2d72b7ee6ac9d5cae24b20e61d831e0c2d250ce7bd5c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T09:26:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/winter-is-coming-putin-seeks-to-hammer-ukrainians-their-power-grid-their-water-supplies--57e07da5252b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/winter-is-coming-putin-seeks-to-hammer-ukrainians-their-power-grid-their-water-supplies" /><summary type="html">As renewed diplomatic efforts seek to bring an end to Russia's war on Ukraine, the prospect of a negotiated settlement remains unlikely due to Russia's irreconcilable territorial demands, competing visions of European security and an increasingly unpredictable and pro-Moscow US. For Mark Galeotti, Executive Director of Mayak Intelligence and Honorary Professor at University College London's School of Slavonic and East European Studies, Moscow's maximalist vision conceals a more complex negotiating strategy. And the territorial dispute over Donbas presents a particularly formidable obstacle. Putin's determination to claim control over the entirety of the region confronts Ukraine's refusal to surrender territory it continues to hold.</summary></entry><entry><title>Europe to send diplomats from across the continent to Ukraine peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:349e60d31cdfee98693faa6e9dd56f834ae9ece4cdfd96b7ba8f7c445ea85ee5</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T01:39:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-live-zelensky-and-kushner-confirm-that-europe-will-join-next-round-of-russia-ukraine-talks--8ff08681f99f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-live-zelensky-and-kushner-confirm-that-europe-will-join-next-round-of-russia-ukraine-talks" /><summary type="html">EU leaders on Friday chose five major powers, including France, Britain, Germany, Italy and Poland, to represent European institutions at the next Ukraine talks. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia using 'illegal and unethical means, knows Europe won't use same means back', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed761f5842a9b319eed407a662b47694af22d6cda546d99e5d905e602493cecb</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:19:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261112-russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says--11000ef3a7f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261112-russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says" /><summary type="html">There are mounting concerns across Europe that recent hoax threats and cyberattacks could be part of a massive hybrid warfare campaign. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Elisabeth Braw, Senior Fellow with the Atlantic Council’s Transatlantic Security Initiative. She says that Russia's aim is to "increase its power at the expense of European countries and the easiest way to do that is to constantly wage this dirty war against European countries, using illegal and unethical means, because Russia knows that we are not going to use the same means back".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Russia using 'illegal and unethical means, knows Europe won't use same means back', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a56b7fbc7d24892616efe691c733b754add493af4270aa03b8fbb9992b7b0ec7</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:12:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says--1a4b49323855.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-using-illegal-and-unethical-means-knows-europe-won-t-use-same-means-back-expert-says" /><summary type="html">There are mounting concerns across Europe that recent hoax threats and cyberattacks could be part of a massive hybrid warfare campaign. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Elisabeth Braw, Senior Fellow with the Atlantic Council’s Transatlantic Security Initiative. She says that Russia's aim is to "increase its power at the expense of European countries and the easiest way to do that is to constantly wage this dirty war against European countries, using illegal and unethical means, because Russia knows that we are not going to use the same means back".</summary></entry><entry><title>Mauritania fishing boats falsely portrayed as migrant fleet bound for Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67ff515e40428d7cd636344a262736f145c3bd0107dacd880d5352fe2b4f9f88</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T21:56:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261112-mauritania-fishing-boats-falsely-portrayed-as-migrant-fleet-bound-for-spain--95715b98438a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261112-mauritania-fishing-boats-falsely-portrayed-as-migrant-fleet-bound-for-spain" /><summary type="html">Spain's Canary Islands are facing renewed pressure from migrant arrivals, with local authorities declaring a state of emergency. Against this backdrop, a viral video claims to show thousands of boats in Mauritania amassing at the port, with users saying they were "ready to set sail" to carry migrants to the archipelago. But the satellite images are misleading: they show a traditional fishing port, not a fleet of migrant vessels. Vedika Bahl explains in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky warns Europe over US-Russia talks on broader security arrangements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a5c7e6f07e964819f54ce97ea79263cfbed5842e83123c45d2de084734c40ea</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T19:53:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-europe-over-us-russia-talks-on-broader-security-arrangements--514193c26030.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-europe-over-us-russia-talks-on-broader-security-arrangements" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned European leaders Thursday to be wary of discussions between the United States and Russia about a new security arrangement for the continent. Before launching the war in 2022, the Kremlin delivered an ultimatum to NATO on Europe's security arrangements which included demands for the alliance to withdraw forces from eastern Europe and stop accepting new members. FRANCE 24's Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's Vladimir Putin suggests no Ukraine compromise in meeting with US envoys</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d82d4c874d263b3e07136d43cc9f7f7dc4ca7724daa3e1daa0aa6db5cf27fde</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-russia-s-vladimir-putin-suggests-no-ukraine-compromise-in-meeting-with-us-envoys--26ef97037a98.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-russia-s-vladimir-putin-suggests-no-ukraine-compromise-in-meeting-with-us-envoys" /><summary type="html">Russia's President Vladimir Putin indicated on Thursday, November 12, that the Kremlin would not compromise on its hardline demands to end the war in Ukraine, but offered a short-term ceasefire in a key frontline city during a meeting with US envoys. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Five men on trial for murder of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci's brother</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4d094a78bb4133f8a12685928e33a8ff4f2c88f91d8715678501a0330912e44</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:20:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother--97c5322846e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother" /><summary type="html">In France, the trial of five men accused of murdering the brother of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci is under way. Amine Kessaci, originally known as an environmental activist, became a prominent figure in the fight against drug-related crime after losing two of his brothers to violence linked to drug trafficking. The defendants face the possibility of life imprisonment. The verdict is expected on Monday, November 16. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>European leaders gather in Dublin to discuss Ukraine's security, and their own</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b32bcd15c2077427f2717f221ac5f2f66c64597ce049016c9f9f9585e5a8b7b</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:19:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-to-discuss-ukraine-s-security-and-their-own--56692e996cbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-to-discuss-ukraine-s-security-and-their-own" /><summary type="html">Leaders from more than 40 European countries gathered in Dublin on Thursday, November 12, for a summit focused on the continent’s fragile security, amid a new US-backed effort to revive talks on ending the Russia-Ukraine war. The meeting of the European Political Community brought together heads of state and government from European countries and the UK, as well as Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney and NATO Secretary-General Mark Rutte.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of schools evacuated in Italy as bomb threats spread across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebee3cc6ef75a3cb782cd682e2157efb62fe7e9c12689cd31175baaf6c26d860</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:08:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-thousands-of-schools-evacuated-in-italy-as-bomb-threats-spread-across-europe--85c832b8d0d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-thousands-of-schools-evacuated-in-italy-as-bomb-threats-spread-across-europe" /><summary type="html">Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". The threats come after a series of hoax bomb alerts across Europe in recent weeks, which have prompted growing concern about the possibility of an escalation in hybrid warfare.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31: Climate disruption puts farmers and global food supplies under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c448a44a1ba2b590a4685c7421640388e2d89874d492b593f6c7f590ec073b59</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:04:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-climate-disruption-puts-farmers-and-global-food-supplies-under-pressure--703bcb8d3e50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-climate-disruption-puts-farmers-and-global-food-supplies-under-pressure" /><summary type="html">As delegates gather in Turkey for the COP31 climate conference, discussions are focusing on emissions and climate targets. But humanitarian agencies are highlighting another urgent consequence of climate disruption: growing food insecurity. With the return of El Niño adding to concerns over extreme weather and its impact on food production, the Food and Agriculture Organisation is calling for food systems to be placed at the heart of climate action.</summary></entry><entry><title>New restrictions to Starshield network 'kill more Ukrainians', Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6718f613c20ec22b354116b2fd28d7ca24b4e34a31ec5c3220b57d5a31a467f4</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:06:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-new-systematic-restrictions-starshield-network-kill-more-ukrainians-zelensky-says--b63c57dc57ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-new-systematic-restrictions-starshield-network-kill-more-ukrainians-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ⁠President Volodymyr Zelensky ​on Thursday said that Ukrainian ​military units had recorded new and significant disruptions to the Starshield satellite communications service in recent days, affecting ​the ‌entire front ⁠line and Russian-occupied parts of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's 'hidden mobilization': The 'expendable' lives fueling Putin's war on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94564427e4b20c34de21898fc4f3a195ad5182ff9c502b1291d87a6f15596277</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:39:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-hidden-mobilization-the-expendable-lives-fueling-putin-s-war-on-ukraine--f5e8509ede95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-hidden-mobilization-the-expendable-lives-fueling-putin-s-war-on-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome John Lough, Senior Research Fellow and Head of Foreign Policy &amp; International Partnerships at the New Eurasian Strategies Centre (NEST Centre), He is also an Associate Fellow with the Russia &amp; Eurasia Programme at Chatham House. Lough offers a sobering assessment of the social and strategic dynamics sustaining Russia's invasion of Ukraine. He argues that the Kremlin has disproportionately recruited soldiers from poorer and politically marginalised communities, including ethnic minority regions, where the human cost of the conflict is less likely to generate organised opposition. Many of those recruited, he explains, "have been recruited for a deliberate reason because they were seen, you know, ultimately as lives that were expendable, in other words as cannon fodder."</summary></entry><entry><title>US envoys arrive in Dublin for meeting with Zelensky and European representatives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b95bc34f5177a00dc7e6f58740b0a142a3a94668bdc5db3dbde628e227c5a42e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T02:31:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks--eb0f36381594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks" /><summary type="html">US special envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner arrived in Dublin Thursday night to meet Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky following their talks with his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin in Moscow. Representatives from France, Germany, Britain and potentially other European nations will also join the discussions, a diplomatic source said. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>European leaders gather in Dublin under the shadow of hybrid threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2d042f82b3c2c8e3ec85fa5e81a4115e91a359dbcb471973f9b887bc3beec54</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T22:46:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-under-the-shadow-of-hybrid-threats--ebbc2bf82ef8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-under-the-shadow-of-hybrid-threats" /><summary type="html">Ireland is mounting the largest security operation in its history as around 50 European leaders gather in Dublin this week amid growing concerns over hybrid attacks. The operation follows a wave of hoax bomb threats targeting airlines and media organisations across Europe, with Irish police reporting new incidents on Monday and Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Olivia Bizot reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine agree to major prisoner swap as peace talks end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73ea7d20644d17652adbed937c2bf79cd0a68204c4ed2d9072a5b056d2def80e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:46:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end--e9c04d147348.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end" /><summary type="html">Kyiv and Moscow on Wednesday agreed to a large-scale prisoner exchange as the final day of peace talks in Abu Dhabi came to an end, though neither side gave a concrete figure. US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will meet separately with Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Ukrainian counterpart Volodymyr Zelensky on Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out hundreds of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c1b83f6570adbf54b3f7e6b861427a3857b611787b96ee5a55d5f6d512c88c2</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain--305c14ca2c0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Millions of workers in Spain shut down businesses and public transport on Wednesday, as part of the country's first general strike in 14 years. Following a peaceful march in Barcelona over soaring rents and property prices, and the rising cost of living, protesters smashed storefronts, set off small bonfires, burned bins and launched fireworks towards police. The unrest comes just weeks before snap elections, called by Socialist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out tens of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ac505c8d44b6d72debb0d222f1e6c7e0245020c80a84edaf9d029b8b3034120</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:37:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain--b3f1fe2dfc35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters marched across Spain on Wednesday during a general strike over housing affordability and purchasing power just weeks before an early general election. Unions reported a significant response in some sectors in Spain's first nationwide 24-hour stoppage since 2012, but business leaders played down the participation. Braving heavy rain, tens of thousands of demonstrators marched through central Madrid carrying placards shaped like houses and chanting "We have no home" as they called for more affordable housing. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands attend Polish nationalist march days after shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26cf7eb5579450e4b987814faafc4f23c2b64a8166d938dc989d027ab4cd9382</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:31:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1--6aff4f4e4234.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Polish nationalist sympathisers gathered in Warsaw Wednesday for an annual Independence Day March, just days after a deadly shooting spree in Krakow that shook the country. The event is held each November 11 to commemorate the ending in 1918 of 123 years of partition by Russia, Prussia and Austria. The event is a magnet for all shades of Poland's right wing -- from conservative-nationalists aligned with its Law and Justice (PiS) party to far-right and radical groups. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Schools evacuated across Italy after bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d8482cad6708a45fb02d0ad0200e516316f431471272f2ca994fcc8a5a12264</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:29:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats--8b8597a1d133.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". Similar hoax threats were reported in schools in Britain and Ireland, which reportedly prompted some evacuations in Scotland. Meloni said she had called a government meeting with security and intelligence chiefs for Wednesday to discuss the threats. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry></feed>
